affiliation with, the upstream owner is claimed.

Third-party: no third-party or vendored code was found in the copied files. audioop-lts (PSF-2.0) is a
declared dependency for Python 3.13 and later; it is not distributed here.

Numbered changes to the source code
D1 engine.py: the find_spec("rasa") type switch is removed; the standalone types are always used.
D2 engine.py: AudioBytes = RasaAudioBytes alias added beside RasaAudioBytes.
D3 base.py, metrics.py, routed_asr.py, routed_tts.py: structlog replaced by the stdlib shim zeo_core.voice._log.
D4 engine.py, base.py, routed_asr.py, routed_tts.py, profile.py: the default name/dotted-path engine factories
   are removed; an EngineFactory is a required argument (build_providers passes the kind to it).
D5 engine.py, base.py: the required_env_vars check and env_present (environment lookups) are removed.
D6 audio.py is unchanged in code; audioop is the standard library on Python 3.12 and audioop-lts on 3.13+.
D7 contract.py: the scanner takes an explicit source root; the rasa import used to find one is removed.
N1-N3 routed_asr.py, routed_tts.py: three inline noqa comments (S110 twice, S311 once), each with a one-line
   reason, on lines whose code is unchanged (each is reviewable in the diff).
Other: __init__.py has a new docstring; _provider_registry.py keeps only the factory contract (the vendor
alias table leaves Core).

